    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s infrastructure program in Vanuatu is supporting the Ministry of Infrastructure and Public Utilities to build climate resilient fiber reinforced concrete roads using local contractors. These roads provide access to services and markets in places where terrain roads have not lasted well in the past. On Nguna Island, home to 1800 people, Australia is constructing a 2.2km concrete road project that is connecting the island&#x2019;s main port to its population centre, up a steep mountain. The road provides all weather access to the island&#x2019;s health center and elementary school and gives farmers reliable access to markets.  It also provides access to the island&#x2019;s dormant volcano, its key tourist attraction. It is being built using two local contractors. A local engineering consultant supervises the works. Forty local workers have been engaged in the project, including six women. This project will deliver real dividends for local commercial activity and the local economy.</narrative>
    </description>
